# **Closing Remarks**

This session covered a broad mix of operational and financial ground: POS session/role handling and the roaming "flying pause" model, the guest application's white-labeling and publishing approach, and an in-depth walkthrough of the finance and ledger architecture — including the dual-ledger data model, per-line VAT and tax-on-tax handling, revenue recognition, a six-step refund flow (extended to include bulk refunds), settlement/reconciliation, and end-to-end financial reporting.  Allam's reference walkthrough of finance-module screens (dashboards, chart of accounts, transactions ledger, revenue recognition rules, payments reconciliation, shift/till management, and reporting) gave the TICVAI team a concrete backend reference to inform their own schema and UI/UX design. The session closed with the AI financial assistant's vector database compliance requirements flagged as time-sensitive ahead of Friday's Dubai Compliance Authority meeting, along with confirmation of Friday's combined infrastructure discussion and workshop covering food & beverage, retail, licensing, and shift management.